{"name":"Airbrushed Copper","hex":"#aa6c51","fetched":"2026-10-20","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"airbrushed","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["simple past and past participle of airbrush"]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having been manipulated with an airbrush.","Having had imperfections and blemishes removed through digital manipulation."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/airbrushed"},{"term":"copper","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A reddish-brown metallic chemical element (symbol Cu) with the atomic number 29; also, the metal made up of this element.","The reddish-brown colour of copper (etymology 1, noun sense 1)."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Made of copper (etymology 1, noun sense 1).","Having the reddish-brown colour of copper."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/copper"}],"entries":[{"title":"Airbrush","blocks":[{"text":"An airbrush is a small, handheld device that uses a stream of compressed air to atomise a liquid and deposit it as a fine spray. Airbrushes are used principally to apply paint, ink and dye, but designs adapted to other materials are also used for cosmetics and decorative finishes. They can produce thin coatings, soft gradations of tone and controlled lines without the direct contact of a conventional brush."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/94/PaascheAirbrush.jpg/330px-PaascheAirbrush.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Airbrush","wikidata":"Q408151"},{"title":"Copper","blocks":[{"text":"Copper is a chemical element; it has symbol Cu and atomic number 29. It is a soft, malleable, and ductile metal with very high thermal and electrical conductivity. A freshly exposed surface of pure copper has a pinkish-orange color. Copper is used as a conductor of heat and electricity, as a building material, and as a constituent of various metal alloys, such as sterling silver used in jewelry, cupronickel used to make marine hardware and coins, and constantan used in strain gauges and thermocouples for temperature measurement."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f0/NatCopper.jpg/330px-NatCopper.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Copper","wikidata":"Q753"},{"title":"Copper (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Copper is a reddish brown color that resembles the metal copper. The first recorded use of copper as a color name in English was in 1594."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d3/Copper-18706.jpg/330px-Copper-18706.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Copper_(color)","wikidata":"Q2722041"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/94/PaascheAirbrush.jpg/500px-PaascheAirbrush.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/94/PaascheAirbrush.jpg/1280px-PaascheAirbrush.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/94/PaascheAirbrush.jpg/500px-PaascheAirbrush.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Paasche F#1 Single-action external mix airbrush","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APaascheAirbrush.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/be/Airbrush_art.jpg/500px-Airbrush_art.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/be/Airbrush_art.jpg/500px-Airbrush_art.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"An Airbrush artist at work","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAirbrush_art.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.or